# Motadata repo + WSL stack testing

When changes are meant to be validated against the **Motadata** workspace using the **WSL** stack (`wsl_plugin_mvp_stack`, Context Layer, `motadata_behavior_verify`, or similar flows described in `docs/guides/MOTADATA_AIOPS_PRODUCTION_VERIFICATION_GUIDE.md`):

1. **Commit** the changes on the machine where the agent applied them (clear message, scoped to the work).
2. **Push** to the remote branch you use on WSL.

**Agent scope:** Do **only** commit and push. Do **not** run `git pull` (or any fetch/merge/rebase) as part of this workflow—that stays on the user’s side when they sync WSL.

**Why push:** Unpushed commits are not on the remote; WSL cannot pick up the agent’s work until it exists on the branch you pull from.

If the agent cannot push (no credentials, blocked network, or user preference), say so explicitly and give the exact `git commit` / `git push` commands to run locally—do not imply the code is already on the remote.

If the user is only iterating locally and has not asked for WSL verification, **do not** add extra commits or pushes solely to satisfy this rule.
